 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d01", "start": 282, "end": 449, "text": "On September 6, 1976 two F-4EJ's of the squadron were scrambled from Chitose to intercept the MiG-25 of Viktor Belenko who had flown into Japanese territory to defect."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d01", "start": 450, "end": 541, "text": "They were unable to intercept him, which led to changes in the Japanese air defense system."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d01", "start": 542, "end": 596, "text": "On November 26, 1985 the squadron transferred to Naha."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d02", "start": 0, "end": 59, "text": "Force squadrons that participated in the Battle of Britain."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d02", "start": 60, "end": 125, "text": "It consisted mostly of Polish pilots, many of whom were veterans."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d02", "start": 126, "end": 316, "text": "The backbone of the squadron was formed by 13 pilots who served with the I/145 Polish Fighter Squadron and were evacuated from France during the last stages of the German invasion of France."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d02", "start": 317, "end": 357, "text": "The squadron was formed on 10 July 1940."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d02", "start": 358, "end": 420, "text": "They piloted some Hawker Hurricanes and were put under the No."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d02", "start": 421, "end": 434, "text": "12 Group RAF."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d02", "start": 435, "end": 519, "text": "As the combat became more fierce, the 302 was moved to RAF Duxford, north of London."}, "D3S8": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0406-cdf455419782:d02", "s